WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:04.460
In Germany, where the cold hits
even harder than in Japan,

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:08.880
they drink their beer at room temperature.
They call it "hot beer".

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:34.550
Tequila, said to be one of the four
great spirits of the world.

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:39.890
A bite of the lime, a lick of salt,
followed by a shot of the tequila.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.930
We call this drinking it "Mexican style".

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.850
But there is another way
to enjoy your drink.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:51.610
Mix club soda with the tequila, place your
hand over the glass and...

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:53.730
slam it on the counter.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:56.860
What a shame.

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.610
We call this the "shotgun".

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.580
And this is what happens
when it goes wrong.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:14.710
As far as drinking in a bar is concerned,
this drink can hardly be called "elegant".

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:20.430
Nevertheless, it is tequila that has come
to epitomise the Mexican drinking style,

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:24.180
tonight's Glass of the Gods,
the Margarita.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:34.190
I see. Mieko Yuzuki is...

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:37.110
I understand.

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:44.950
Ibsen's "A Doll's House".

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:53.830
Seems I will never
get to see it after all.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:04.800
Hey, was that...?

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:07.640
Yes. He is from Shimaoka advertising.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.400
But I understand he is retiring
as president tomorrow.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.360
He seems lonely considering
it's the night before his departure.

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:22.410
As far as the many bars in Ginza are
concerned, this is a night like any other.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:25.870
For the ones with regular patrons,

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:27.740
every evening and at the same time,

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:31.960
there are those who come to enjoy
the same drink, in the same seat.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:36.210
When this goes on for ten
or even twenty years,

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:39.710
the bar will keep the seat reserved
and wait for the customer to arrive.

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:46.930
There are, however,

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:51.640
some evenings when unusual events occur,
which break those unspoken rules.

00:03:57.690 --> 00:03:59.900
Good evening, Mr Shimaoka.

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:04.160
It is unusual to see you
here at such a time.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:06.200
I'm sorry to inconvenience you

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:09.410
but would you mind waiting here
until your seat becomes available?

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.120
That'll be fine.

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.460
"Mixed drinks"?

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:25.720
Yes. It seems I mistakenly took it
with me from the last bar.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:28.680
I'll have to return it later.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.520
I may be a drinker but I have manners.

00:04:34.060 --> 00:04:36.690
I've lived my whole life
trying to be well-mannered.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.730
But tonight, I've already broken
three of the bar-goer's Ten Commandments.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.490
The bar-goer's Ten Commandments.

00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:45.360
Indeed.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:49.450
He got into a fight with the patron
next to him at the first bar.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.540
And drank too much at the second.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:56.920
And at the third bar...

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:06.470
Here, at the third bar,
where I am a regular customer,

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:09.010
I'm about to get drunk and go on a rant.

00:05:09.430 --> 00:05:12.680
How about a light bite in that case?

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:18.020
No... I heard today that someone
I once cared for passed away.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.690
I feel like getting drunk.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.780
Do you know the stage actress, Mieko Yuzuki?

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:28.110
I do. She's famous, is she not?

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.410
Did she pass away?

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:30.410
She did.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:35.290
A DOLL'S HOUSE

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:38.540
A Doll's House... As it turns out, I never got to see her perform even once.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:38.710
As it turns out, I never got to see
her perform even once.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.130
I was always so swamped with work...

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.840
The truth is, I'm about to retire,

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:48.430
I should be leaving my job with pride
but somehow I feel empty inside.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:54.010
It makes me question whether my life
so far has meant anything at all.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:56.020
Or was it all just pointless...?

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:57.730
Pointless?

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:00.440
Ah, now I've broken the fourth taboo.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.070
Drinking at bars out of self-pity
is forbidden, am I right?

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:06.360
Give me something strong
that'll lift my spirits.

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.070
Very well, sir.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.390
A Margarita.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:53.410
I usually have a high ball.

00:06:53.530 --> 00:06:55.870
So I'm not normally one for cocktails.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.460
This is delicious!

00:07:05.500 --> 00:07:09.970
And the name is that of a lady,
am I right?

00:07:10.380 --> 00:07:11.050
It is.

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:23.190
The Margarita was created in 1949,
at the All-American Cocktail Contest.

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.980
The man to showcase it came
from a Los Angeles restaurant.

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:31.070
The Tail O' the Cock's bartender,
John Durlesser.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:41.710
In his past, as a young man, he went
hunting with his girlfriend

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:46.130
who sadly was hit by
a stray bullet and died.

00:07:53.510 --> 00:07:56.050
The name he gave his cocktail,
the Margarita,

00:07:56.180 --> 00:08:00.890
was the name of his lover,
who died 23 years prior.

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:07.400
One can only assume he had never been
able to forget his long lost-love.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:16.030
The feelings of regret one bartender
held onto all those years,

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:18.450
gave birth to this cocktail.

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:24.040
So perhaps we can say that his past,
so full of regret, wasn't without meaning.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:27.040
Such a bittersweet story.

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.170
Quite.

00:08:28.790 --> 00:08:31.840
In memory of this girlfriend,
who was Mexican,

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:34.880
he kept the Mexican element
in his cocktail.

00:08:35.840 --> 00:08:38.100
Which element is Mexican?

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:41.390
It's a strong drink but would
you like to try it?

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:47.270
You put the salt on your hand and
hold the lime like so.

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:52.190
You hold the shot glass containing
the tequila between your fingers.

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:56.490
Take a bit of the lime, then lick the salt
and finally drink the tequila.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.740
This is called "Mexican style",

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:03.250
and the cocktail that best
represents it is the Margarita.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:04.960
I see.

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:07.330
The salt lining the edge of the glass,

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:11.250
and the lime mixed in with the tequila
coming together are reminiscent of that.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:16.090
Younger customers have
a drink they call the "shotgun".

00:09:16.220 --> 00:09:21.140
You mix soda with tequila, slam it on
the counter and then neck it back.

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:36.110
Would you like to try?

00:09:38.660 --> 00:09:40.700
Neither the Mexican style nor the shotgun

00:09:40.870 --> 00:09:44.500
are especially elegant
ways of drinking at a bar,

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:46.120
but I'd be happy to make you one.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:49.210
Thanks, but I'll pass.

00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:51.960
Trying out new things...

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:56.510
having new experiences...
I'm too old for all that, now.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:01.300
First of all, my past isn't so beautifuI

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:04.720
that it should merit being
likened to a spirit.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.230
Now, now, Nora... or should I say,
my little bird.

00:10:13.360 --> 00:10:16.190
There's no need to let
your wings droop so.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:18.450
Or have they recoiled in fear?

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:24.660
Ah, I see. But then again,
maybe you'll perk up once you see this...

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:29.870
I thought that might surprise you.

00:10:31.250 --> 00:10:34.630
Listen. I've become a great success.

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:36.630
I run a bank now.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:44.600
Those were the lines
from her favourite play.

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:47.310
Ibsen's "A Doll's House".

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:51.980
Come to think of it,
I never told you, did I?

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:56.940
There was, in fact, a time in my youth
when I dreamt of becoming an actor.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:00.900
It's a bit embarrassing but
I can still memorise lines.

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:07.410
I haven't forgotten... It was at
the peak of Japan's rapid economic growth.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:12.290
Both Ginza and I were still young.

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:14.500
My father put up billboards
all over the town,

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:15.960
RM COSMETICS... My father
put up billboards all over the town,

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:16.040
My father put up billboards
all over the town,

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:19.630
which was growing into a metropolis
at an unimaginable speed,

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:24.390
as he tried to lay the grounds for
a large advertising company.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:29.470
It meant that I was able to do
as I pleased without want for anything.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:33.190
During my time of carefree abandon,
I went to see a popular show

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:35.770
which utterly enthralled me.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:41.240
It was "A Doll's House".

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:46.070
I had seen many films and read
all kinds of books, before then.

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:49.490
But never had I seen anything
that captivated me this much.

00:11:50.500 --> 00:11:55.290
And the person I went to see it with
was Mieko Yuzuki, who since passed away.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:01.300
We wasted no time in knocking on
the theatre troupe's door.

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:14.650
Alas, as you can see,

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:18.270
I was not destined to become a thespian,

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:22.070
and standing on stage would remain
no more than a pipe dream.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.790
But, as it turned out, not for her...

00:12:35.370 --> 00:12:36.710
You're quitting acting?

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:42.210
Yeah... My father's getting worse.

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:47.090
So you're breaking up with me
to take over your father's company as CEO.

00:12:47.300 --> 00:12:50.100
That's not it! You've got it wrong...

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:53.100
And what about our dream then?

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:58.230
What about our dream of
standing on the stage together?

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:03.110
What about our dream of performing
in Ibsen's "A Doll House" together?

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:10.330
Please understand...

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:13.660
We can't all live by chasing our dreams!

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:21.420
After I broke up with her,
I took over my father's company,

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:25.090
and took the Company, Shimaoka
Advertising, to the top of the industry.

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:29.090
From tomorrow, my son
will be entrusted with the company

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:30.890
and I will retire.

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:36.730
When I look back, our company handled
the advertising for so many products.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:39.770
Smoking and its impact on health.

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:43.570
COLD LIPS
RM COSMETICS LIPSTICK
Cosmetics worn by all women.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:47.400
A RIDE THAT OUTCLASSES THE REST! SKYMARK GTX

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:52.740
To me they were also
proof of my personal growth.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:58.920
But the only adverts we never handled
were those for films or plays.

00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:05.760
I guess I avoided them for fear of bumping
into the woman who'd succeeded in theatre.

00:14:06.470 --> 00:14:10.930
But she never stopped sending me tickets
to the show for the last 50 years.

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:14.010
"A Doll's House" by Ibsen.

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:17.310
The same play that we saw
together for the first time.

00:14:17.430 --> 00:14:18.940
Showing tomorrow...

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:24.400
But, in the end, I still
won't be able to go see it.

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:28.240
At the end of this story,

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:33.030
the heroine, Nora, leaves her husband,
freeing herself from his adulation,

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:37.290
and Mr Helmer is left with only
his "success" to keep him company.

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:46.420
What sits before me

00:14:46.460 --> 00:14:50.130
is a glass poured for a lover
who died over 20 years ago.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.760
And it is filled with memories of regret.

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:57.810
What a clichéd phoney story...

00:14:58.270 --> 00:14:59.600
A phoney story?

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:02.310
Who would believe a story like that?

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:06.440
A load of poppycock made up by a liquor
store or a bartender, to sell Margaritas.

00:15:07.280 --> 00:15:11.070
Have you heard of dramatised commercials?

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:16.540
It's my job to know about them from my
work in the advertising industry.

00:15:17.620 --> 00:15:19.500
"Dramatised commercials".

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:22.710
An advertising strategy
with a long history.

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:27.590
It is a method of selling that adds drama
to a product by creating a made-up story

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:31.010
around the development of the product.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:35.970
It even makes the consumer more
susceptible to dreams about the product.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:39.430
However, in the case of the Margarita...

00:15:40.730 --> 00:15:42.140
You could be right.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:44.730
It all seems a bit far-fetched.

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:46.860
Sorry.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.690
It's okay. It isn't your fault.

00:15:51.190 --> 00:15:54.740
But, if it is indeed
no more than fiction...

00:15:56.950 --> 00:15:57.990
I will go home.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:01.370
Yes, sir.

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:16.550
Good heavens, man...

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:20.430
The bar's Ten Commandments.
How many did I break tonight?

00:16:20.520 --> 00:16:24.640
"Thou shalt not raise thy voice
and lecture young bartenders."

00:16:28.570 --> 00:16:30.070
Margarita...

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:34.400
A cocktail for a dead lover, was it?
Ridiculous.

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:37.490
Is it, though?

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.000
What are you trying to tell me?

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.420
When are you going to disappear
from my sight already?

00:16:46.750 --> 00:16:51.090
I just don't want to regret
anything further.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.420
That is all.

00:16:54.050 --> 00:16:55.430
What?

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:30.670
The birth of the Margarita.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.170
It was decades later that
the story was found out.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:38.720
Indeed. 1970...

00:17:38.930 --> 00:17:44.310
Thirty years after the contest,
John Durlesser, who created the cocktail,

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:49.810
finally told the media that he had named
the drink after his dead lover.

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:56.820
In other words, the story was not
made up in order to boost sales.

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.530
For fifty years...

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:03.080
all those tickets you sent me...

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:07.370
I had shut them in the past,
as if I couldn't see them.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:10.830
You must have thought me so heartless.

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:15.420
But I finally understood clearly
when I drank that Margarita.

00:18:16.010 --> 00:18:18.510
The fact is that I was afraid.

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:21.760
Afraid to face myself from the past,
the person who betrayed you.

00:18:22.140 --> 00:18:26.140
Because, just like the bartender
who created the Margarita,

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:29.310
I wasn't courageous enough
to look at the past.

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:33.060
But now I understand...

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:38.450
It is because I've done everything I could
not to lose to my regrets,

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.870
that my company came
to be accepted by the world.

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:44.870
And while you made
a success out of your Iife,

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:48.370
I too was able to live mine on my terms.

00:18:49.290 --> 00:18:50.580
That's right.

00:18:51.120 --> 00:18:53.500
A past with regrets is not
one that's meaningless.

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:56.840
I am the man I am today
because of my regrets!

00:18:57.550 --> 00:19:01.760
That is what young Sasakura,
the bartender, was trying to tell me!

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:20.400
Being a bartender is a peculiar job.

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:26.200
For example, a company CEO would never
discuss his issues with a new hire.

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:30.960
However, in a bar, every customer goes
back to being a simple human being.

00:19:33.210 --> 00:19:37.250
The reason being that although
the customer is speaking to us,

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:42.090
they are in fact speaking to their own
heart and to their own past.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:45.430
Bars are places
where such things are possible.

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:48.680
Which is why a bartender's main job

00:19:48.810 --> 00:19:50.890
is listening to customers.

00:19:51.520 --> 00:19:55.440
Stories about spirits are no more than
ice breakers to start a conversation.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:09.990
Speaking to one's heart and one's past.

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:14.370
Thanks to that, finally you and I
understand each other.

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:31.980
One more Margarita.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:40.980
Actually, I think I'll take you up
on your earlier suggestion, first...

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:13.100
RECIPE: TEQUILA - 40ml COINTREAU - 5ml
LIME JUICE - 15ml SALT - To Taste

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:28.680
Translation & Adaptation: Christopher Ward Proofreading: Andrew Cull WAKANIM

00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:33.930
